WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.370
(barking)

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.472
MATT: This whole house
is fear and violence.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:07.473
If these guys don't do the work,

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:09.275 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're probably gonna
get a dog killed.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.244 align:start position:0%
BRYANT: The bulldogs are getting
more and more aggressive

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.311
towards each other.

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.614
RIDDHI: Pax bit his forearm.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.614
(barking)

00:00:15.614 --> 00:00:17.383
MATT: This dog is a powder keg.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.018
(growling)

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.354
Easy, please. It's okay.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.856
Okay.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.989
STEF: Just look at
his whole demeanor.

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:25.891
MATT: He is scared and
he doesn't have somebody

00:00:25.891 --> 00:00:27.861
that's standing up for him.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:30.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want him to get in
movement and rhythm with me.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.298
You just haven't been
taught social manners.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.701
There we go. Good boy.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.170
(barking)

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm Matt Beisner, and I work
with aggressive dogs.

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
I promise you
I'm not trying to hurt you.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.309 align:start size:91% position:9%
I take the dogs
other people won't touch.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:47.080
You do not want to be a monster.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.983
And rehabilitate them with
respect, trust and love.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.719 align:start size:88% position:13%
WOMAN: I cannot believe
how calm he is.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:57.690
MATT: Because I know
there are no bad dogs.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.560
♪ ♪

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:08.234
♪ ♪

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
I'm on my way in to work
with a dog named Pax, P-A-X.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.241 line:0%
Ironically enough, his name
is supposed to mean peace.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.144
He has at least one bite.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.346
Apparently they can't have
anybody come in the home

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.915
unless he's on muzzle.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
My process with dogs usually
begins with a house call.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.485
I come into your home,

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.919 align:start size:91% position:9%
it's about two and a half,
three hours.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want to sit with you,
listen to you,

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.057 align:start size:88% position:13%
observe what's happening
with your dog,

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.992
and then things just
evolve from there.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:36.128 align:start size:91% position:9%
I don't know how dangerous
Pax is really gonna be

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:37.831
until I meet him.

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:42.835 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
RIDDHI: We have two dogs,
Pax and Emma,

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.004
and Pax is the problem child.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.240 align:start size:81% position:19%
RAYHAN: Anything can
make him snap.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:51.410 line:0%
(barking)

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.147 align:start size:84% position:16%
RIDDHI: I feel
very attached to him.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.048 align:start position:0%
RAYHAN: Starting at three months
we started to see issues,

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.617
nipping at people.

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.786 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then at four months
he bit somebody.

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:03.189
After that, there were
other incidents as well.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's always a chance
that he might bite someone.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.460
(barking)

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.962 align:start size:81% position:19%
RIDDHI: It's really,
really dire.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:12.665 align:start size:97% position:3%
We need to get Pax help,
and it needs to be right now.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.466
(knocking)

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.034
(barking)

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.502 align:start size:88% position:13%
MATT: Hi.
RIDDHI: Hi. How are you?

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.137 align:start size:81% position:19%
MATT: Matt Beisner.
Who's this one?

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.005
RAYHAN: This is Emma.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:19.972
MATT: Hi, Emma.

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:21.240
Let's just sit down and...

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.976
(barking)

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:27.246
Generally what I'm getting
when I walk into a house,

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.749 align:start size:91% position:9%
I'm tall, I shave my head,
I wear dark clothes.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:33.085
I know I'm basically
a walking trigger.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:36.889 align:start size:91% position:9%
90% of aggression in dogs
is fear based.

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:38.557
And knowing that,
the question is

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.660 align:start size:88% position:13%
how do I set this dog up
to feel safe?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.263 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm not gonna hurt you,
and you're not gonna hurt me.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.331
Okay?

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.266
Clearly he's pretty scared,

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.935 align:start size:91% position:9%
and it looks like he could
be really dangerous.

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:51.604
How old was he when you got him?

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
RAYHAN: He was really small.
RIDDHI: One month.

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:53.772
RAYHAN: Yeah, one month.

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:55.274
MATT: Four weeks old?
RIDDHI: Four weeks old.

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:56.842
RAYHAN: Yeah, actually
we found him online,

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.911
and when we went there,
it was really sketchy.

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:01.147 align:start size:88% position:13%
RIDDHI: His mom was like
pretty emaciated.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.982
RAYHAN: We actually didn't
want to take him that early.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:97% position:3%
We wanted to give him at least
two months with his mom.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start position:0%
But they were like,
"We need to get rid of him now,

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.821
and if you don't want him,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.956 align:start size:88% position:13%
we're going to give him
to someone else."

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.925 align:start position:0%
MATT: You may be the only people
that I've worked with

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.759 align:start size:78% position:22%
that got a dog
at four weeks old.

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:14.927
If dogs don't get what they need

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.829 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the first 10 weeks
of development,

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.864
the brain doesn't wire properly.

00:03:18.864 --> 00:03:22.701
And that you got him from
a really dicey situation,

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:23.869
at the very least neglected,

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:26.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
if not actually abused
or watching abuse.

00:03:26.071 --> 00:03:28.641
It makes sense that
he would display

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:32.645 align:start size:84% position:16%
the kind of aggression
that he has.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:33.846 align:start size:78% position:22%
Do you want to get
that muzzle off

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:37.216
so you can let me know what
you really think about this?

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.318
Clearly Pax has some
stunted development

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.020
that has left him
crippled with fear

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.689
and left him no skills
to deal with that stress.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.559
Ultimately, that can manifest
in violence and aggression.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.261
(barking)

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.932
Have you had incidents
in the home with him

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.032
where he's bitten people?

00:03:54.032 --> 00:03:55.701 align:start size:91% position:9%
RAYHAN: There was one time
with each of us;

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.703
he bit my arm once
and then with her.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:58.604
RIDDHI: Upper leg.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:03:59.939
MATT: Uh-huh. Did it puncture?

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.274
RIDDHI: Yeah.

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.176
RAYHAN: Unfortunately
there was one time,

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:05.778
my friend was telling a story,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he got animated and
put his hands up like this.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:08.715
MATT: Uh-huh.

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.582 align:start size:81% position:19%
RAYHAN: And Pax just
like lunged.

00:04:10.582 --> 00:04:12.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
MATT: Was it like a one-two
or did he go?

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.954 align:start position:0%
RAYHAN: Yeah, it was a one-two.
It was...

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.122 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: There's the hands thing
you were talking about.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:16.922
RIDDHI: Right.
RAYHAN: Yeah.

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.090
MATT: Okay.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.025 align:start position:0%
It can be agonizing for
the owners during a home visit,

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:22.194 align:start size:84% position:16%
like I'm just here
setting off their dog,

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:24.230 align:start size:91% position:9%
but in reality I'm getting
key information.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.430
What are the dog's triggers?

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.200
What's the threshold for stress?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.705 align:start size:91% position:9%
RAYHAN: We feel very stuck
in life and with him.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:33.806
(sighs)

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:34.974
I feel bad.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.575
It's like he just puts this
like darkness on everything,

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:38.144
and it's not his fault.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:41.046
We care about him so much and
we have a very strong feeling

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:45.251
that if we give him up, that
he'll probably get put down.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:47.786
MATT: Yeah.

00:04:47.786 --> 00:04:49.321
Rayhan's not wrong about this.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.724
The majority of the dogs that
get put down in Los Angeles

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.192
are pits and pit bull mixes,

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:56.896
so turning this around for Pax
is a matter of life or death.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.766 align:start size:97% position:3%
I want to move to
a different experience for him

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:04.403
and that is with me sitting
here, but other than that,

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:06.405 align:start size:88% position:13%
I just want to see
what it's like for him.

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:08.675 align:start size:81% position:19%
It gives me a place
to start from.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.346
Stay there for a moment.

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:16.182
Okay.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.417 align:start size:88% position:13%
Give me the long end
of the leash. Thank you.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.086 align:start size:84% position:16%
Okay, there it is,
there's the stillness,

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:22.321 align:start size:81% position:19%
and now he's,
there goes the ears.

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.456
Right, he's ready to pop at me.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:26.492
Pax has been barking
and growling at me,

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.494
but now he's gone
still and silent,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:31.297 align:start size:97% position:3%
which for a lot of dogs
means they're about to attack.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.031 align:start size:84% position:16%
He's definitely trying
to work an angle.

00:05:33.031 --> 00:05:35.968
Hand me that long end of
the leash behind your back.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.670 align:start size:91% position:9%
And I promise you
I'm not here to hurt you.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.405
Okay, let go. I got it.

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:44.143
I don't want to hurt you.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:46.245
I just want to see
what we can do, okay?

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
In order to help defuse
Pax's aggression towards me,

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.716 align:start size:78% position:22%
I approach him
with a calm energy

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:52.218
and a non-threatening manner.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.919
Let's sit down.

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.088
We gotta do this together. Okay?

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want him to read my energy
and downshift.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.827
There's the stillness that
his pupils are so dilated.

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:04.330
Yeah, you want to lunge at me
when I sit down, don't you?

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.832 align:start size:91% position:9%
But he's still seeing red
and he can't learn

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:09.502 align:start size:88% position:13%
when he's in that state
and being edgy.

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.803
Yeah, it's too much.

00:06:11.803 --> 00:06:15.308 align:start size:97% position:3%
He's one of the more dangerous
dogs that I've worked with.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.610
Definitely.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.877
It's not gonna happen.

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:20.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're just gonna keep going
through the same thing,

00:06:20.545 --> 00:06:22.281
and it's gonna create
more stress for him.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.984
I'd you to put him back in.

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:31.557
(barking)

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:36.195
Good boy, Pax.

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:39.298
Good boy, Pax.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:41.733
I'll take that.

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:44.236 align:start size:84% position:16%
Pax chose to downshift
and lay down.

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:45.404
It's small but it's a win,

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:47.640
and at this point we need
to keep reinforcing that.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:52.311 align:start position:0%
I'd be very detached about
how and when he gets affection.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.512
You've gotta wait
till he's calm.

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:56.815
As long as he stays calm,
you can keep petting him.

00:06:56.815 --> 00:06:59.885 align:start size:88% position:13%
Neurologically,
I want him to understand

00:06:59.885 --> 00:07:03.722 align:start size:84% position:16%
that when you are calm
and you stay calm,

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:06.259 align:start size:97% position:3%
we will give you all
the affection you can handle,

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:10.029 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you are going to reinforce
what he needs most

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:13.332
to be able to stand a chance to
go out and change in the world,

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:15.468
which is his ability
to calm himself down.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:17.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Next steps, we've gotta get
Pax out of the home

00:07:17.836 --> 00:07:20.339 align:start size:97% position:3%
and into the Zen yard
to socialize with other dogs.

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.575
And then we can use that
as a bridge to get him back

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:25.778 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the home safely interacting
with other people.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:27.246 align:start size:84% position:16%
RIDDHI: We really need
Matt's help.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
RAYHAN: It's like every day
is another chance

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:32.150
that something bad might happen
and we have to put him down.

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:34.954
RIDDHI: That is kind of like our
last resort and our last hope.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:36.689
MATT: Alright, kid,
I'm gonna walk by.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.825
(barking)
That a boy.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.196 line:0%
(barking)

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:45.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
I want to talk
about the presidents.

00:07:45.597 --> 00:07:48.166
They are five bulldogs
named after presidents.

00:07:48.166 --> 00:07:50.936
In the home there is
such regular fighting

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:54.707
that the owner has
a fight breakup stick

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:55.907
on the couch next to him.

00:07:55.907 --> 00:07:58.577
The dogs break into a fight and
he pulls the break stick out,

00:07:58.577 --> 00:07:59.845
breaks it up, puts them back.

00:07:59.845 --> 00:08:00.846
This is a regular occurrence,

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.382
but they're actually
puncturing each other,

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:07.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the owners have been bit
breaking up the fights.

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:09.121
WOMAN: Are they all rescues?

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:11.290 align:start size:88% position:13%
MATT: Some rescues,
some come from breeders.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.158 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm gonna do a private session
with them

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:15.094
and we will have them coming in.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:15.895
Cool?

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:21.767
(barking)

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:23.435
BRYANT: Calm down, please.

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:25.170 line:0%
I'm Bryant and this is Justin,

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.006 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and we are the parents
of five bulldogs.

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:30.809 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:36.448 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:08:36.448 --> 00:08:37.950 align:start size:84% position:16%
JUSTIN: The five dogs
are our children,

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
we love their big paws
and their big fur and rolls,

00:08:41.586 --> 00:08:44.322
and I just love having
these hippos run around

00:08:44.322 --> 00:08:46.592
and knock you over in the house.

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:50.830
The problem now is
as the days go on,

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.798
the bulldogs are getting
more and more aggressive

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:54.433
towards each other.

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:56.801
(barking)

00:08:56.801 --> 00:08:58.470
You think they're okay at times,

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.505 align:start size:81% position:19%
but then within
a snap of a finger,

00:09:00.505 --> 00:09:02.408
they lunge towards each other.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:05.811
(barking)

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
BRYANT: We're concerned about
the dogs' safety

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:09.348
and our own safety

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:12.017 align:start size:91% position:9%
when they are aggressively
going after each other.

00:09:12.017 --> 00:09:14.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we're also worried about
other people's safety

00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:15.888
that come to the house.

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:21.293 line:0%
JUSTIN: Right now we don't feel
totally comfortable in our home;

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:23.762 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're always tensed up
and stressed

00:09:23.762 --> 00:09:26.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
and not knowing what's
gonna happen next.

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:29.634
Dog room's on the right here.

00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:30.636
MATT: Okay, cool.

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:33.572 align:start size:88% position:13%
Do you have the ones
that are prone to fight?

00:09:33.572 --> 00:09:34.907 align:start size:91% position:9%
BRYANT: They're separated
in that room.

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:36.208 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: They're separated? Okay.
BRYANT: Yeah.

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:39.011 line:0%
BRYANT: So I tend to think it's
more Roosevelt who starts it.

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:42.047 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
Eisenhower will back off,
go into a corner,

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:45.951 align:start size:84% position:16%
so he then jumps first
and then it starts.

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:48.820
(barking)

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:51.089 align:start size:91% position:9%
Truman, the youngest one,
when we adopted him,

00:09:51.089 --> 00:09:54.326 line:0%
he was a calm puppy,
very nice and gentle.

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:57.229 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
He's now starting to jump
into those fights.

00:09:57.229 --> 00:09:59.832
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:09:59.832 --> 00:10:00.933
It gets a little scary.

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:02.167
There was one time he bit me

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:04.636 align:start size:91% position:9%
because he was right here
and drew blood.

00:10:04.636 --> 00:10:06.805
MATT: Stability needs
to happen in this home.

00:10:06.805 --> 00:10:08.307
If these guys don't do the work,

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:10.276 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're probably gonna
get a dog killed.

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:13.479
Really the issue is between
Roosevelt and Eisenhower,

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:15.848 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it creates a madness
amongst the five.

00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:19.585
BRYANT: All day long is
barking, aggressiveness.

00:10:19.585 --> 00:10:20.686
MATT: Alright.

00:10:20.686 --> 00:10:22.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
BRYANT: It takes a toll
on like our personal lives.

00:10:22.921 --> 00:10:25.991
MATT: That sounds
really stressful.

00:10:25.991 --> 00:10:28.727 align:start position:0%
It sounds like Murdock and
Lincoln are innocent bystanders

00:10:28.727 --> 00:10:30.329
to this dangerous dynamic

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:33.231 align:start position:0%
that's happening with Roosevelt,
Truman and Eisenhower,

00:10:33.231 --> 00:10:35.234 align:start size:91% position:9%
so I want to look at these
three troublemakers

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:37.235 align:start size:84% position:16%
and see what's really
happening here.

00:10:37.235 --> 00:10:39.472 align:start size:91% position:9%
Alright, we're gonna play
this one at a time.

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:40.272
BRYANT: Okay.

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:42.641
MATT: And I want the two of you

00:10:42.641 --> 00:10:45.611
to ignore the dog
completely, okay?

00:10:45.611 --> 00:10:47.613 align:start size:88% position:13%
The first step to seeing
what the problem is,

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:51.050
is teaching Bryant and Justin
how to detach from their dogs.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:52.851
I start with Roosevelt
since he's getting blamed

00:10:52.851 --> 00:10:54.286
for a lot of the fighting.

00:10:54.286 --> 00:10:57.256
Let's bring the tormentor out.

00:10:57.256 --> 00:10:59.458 align:start position:0% line:0%
Always when I come into the home
I ask the humans

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:01.727 align:start position:0% line:0%
to ignore the dogs,
'cause I want to see two things:

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:03.495
what does the dog
do with its humans,

00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:06.065
and what's the dog do
with the stranger.

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:08.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
The right side of the face,
is that...

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:10.035 align:start position:0%
JUSTIN: That's from Eisenhower.
MATT: Yeah.

00:11:10.035 --> 00:11:12.604 align:start size:84% position:16%
JUSTIN: That's exactly
where they bite.

00:11:12.604 --> 00:11:13.505
MATT: Thank you, Roosevelt.

00:11:13.505 --> 00:11:15.107 align:start size:81% position:19%
We'll see you in
a little bit, buddy.

00:11:15.107 --> 00:11:17.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, his own, Roosevelt seems
like a typical bulldog,

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:19.978
but there's something in his
relationship with his owners

00:11:19.978 --> 00:11:22.648
and the other dogs that's
driving him to aggression.

00:11:22.648 --> 00:11:24.883
I'll bring Truman out.

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:27.218
Just gotta give us some space.
Come on out, kiddo. Come on.

00:11:27.218 --> 00:11:28.387
BRYANT: He's the skittish one.

00:11:28.387 --> 00:11:29.355
MATT: Yeah.

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:30.389
Come on, Truman.

00:11:30.389 --> 00:11:31.523 align:start size:88% position:13%
JUSTIN: He has
a questionable history,

00:11:31.523 --> 00:11:33.058
whereas we first
brought him home,

00:11:33.058 --> 00:11:34.693
he wouldn't even
leave his kennel.

00:11:34.693 --> 00:11:36.261
You could tell he was afraid.

00:11:36.261 --> 00:11:37.862 align:start size:84% position:16%
MATT: Come on, Truman.
Come on out.

00:11:37.862 --> 00:11:39.932
You want to see what
we're doing out here?

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:43.635
I'm just here to help you.

00:11:43.635 --> 00:11:47.706
It sounds like things
are a little bit scary.

00:11:47.706 --> 00:11:49.174
Let's go see what's out there.

00:11:49.174 --> 00:11:51.143
Let's go check it out, come on.

00:11:51.143 --> 00:11:52.611
We're gonna take
a walk together.

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:53.545
Here's what we're gonna do.

00:11:53.545 --> 00:11:54.813 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm not gonna make you
do anything,

00:11:54.813 --> 00:11:55.914
but we're gonna see about

00:11:55.914 --> 00:11:58.417 align:start size:91% position:9%
getting out in this world
together, okay?

00:11:58.417 --> 00:12:00.219
Come on, let's keep walking.

00:12:00.219 --> 00:12:02.854
I'll walk with you.

00:12:02.854 --> 00:12:03.956
I can see you're scared.

00:12:03.956 --> 00:12:05.791
Oh, my buddy.

00:12:05.791 --> 00:12:07.259
I can see you're scared.

00:12:07.259 --> 00:12:09.994 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm struck by how afraid
Truman is.

00:12:09.994 --> 00:12:12.297
Truman is crippled with fear;

00:12:12.297 --> 00:12:14.499
all he wants to do is
get back to his crate.

00:12:14.499 --> 00:12:16.435
It's kind of heartbreaking.

00:12:16.435 --> 00:12:18.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bulldogs are not aggressive
by nature,

00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:20.339 align:start size:84% position:16%
but if they're not
socialized as puppies,

00:12:20.339 --> 00:12:22.274 align:start size:91% position:9%
it's likely they're gonna
become aggressive.

00:12:22.274 --> 00:12:24.343
His training is gonna be
about getting comfortable

00:12:24.343 --> 00:12:26.011 align:start size:88% position:13%
and being able to trust
in the world.

00:12:26.011 --> 00:12:28.113 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
My next move is
to bring Eisenhower out.

00:12:28.113 --> 00:12:31.083 align:start position:0% line:0%
Let's go sit down on the couch,
see what happens.

00:12:34.687 --> 00:12:36.222
Hi.

00:12:37.823 --> 00:12:39.792
Okay.

00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:41.026 align:start size:66% position:34%
(barking)
Yeah.

00:12:41.026 --> 00:12:42.127
BRYANT: Eisen.

00:12:42.127 --> 00:12:46.131
(barking)

00:12:46.131 --> 00:12:48.700 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: A lot of fear,
these dogs have a lot of fear.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.803
Do you have any concern that
he would lunge at the cameras?

00:12:51.803 --> 00:12:53.905
JUSTIN: I don't think
immediately. I think...

00:12:53.905 --> 00:12:57.008 align:start size:88% position:13%
MATT: Tss! Easy, please.
It's okay.

00:12:57.008 --> 00:12:59.512
JUSTIN: Eisen, no. Eisen, no.

00:13:03.948 --> 00:13:05.851 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
JUSTIN: Eisen, no. Eisen, no.
MATT: Okay.

00:13:05.851 --> 00:13:07.051 align:start size:88% position:13%
MATT: Eisenhower's fear
is pushing him

00:13:07.051 --> 00:13:08.586
towards the edge of violence.

00:13:08.586 --> 00:13:11.457
That's the theme of this whole
house, is fear and violence.

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:13.191
In a multi-dog household,

00:13:13.191 --> 00:13:15.460
a secure pack creates
a safe environment.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.363
In a home like this,
the sketchy backgrounds

00:13:17.363 --> 00:13:19.431
of some of these dogs,
combined with insecurity,

00:13:19.431 --> 00:13:21.667 align:start size:88% position:13%
means there's jockeying
for position.

00:13:21.667 --> 00:13:23.936
(barking)

00:13:23.936 --> 00:13:26.672
Go ahead and get him back.

00:13:26.672 --> 00:13:28.540
JUSTIN: Come on.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: The relationship between
these three dogs is toxic.

00:13:31.276 --> 00:13:35.480
There are varying degrees of
anxiety and fear in this home,

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.482
and the fear that
is the strongest

00:13:37.482 --> 00:13:39.318 align:start size:81% position:19%
is what leads to
the most aggression.

00:13:39.318 --> 00:13:40.352
JUSTIN: Yeah.

00:13:40.352 --> 00:13:42.888 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: So if we create
more security in the home,

00:13:42.888 --> 00:13:46.592 align:start size:91% position:9%
then there is less
of a reason to be afraid.

00:13:46.592 --> 00:13:49.695 align:start position:0%
BRYANT: Overall I was surprised
to find out how much fear

00:13:49.695 --> 00:13:52.965 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
the dogs do have
in causing the fights.

00:13:52.965 --> 00:13:54.733 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: So, there's a few things
I want to see happen

00:13:54.733 --> 00:13:55.901
in the next month.

00:13:55.901 --> 00:13:57.135
There's no incident.

00:13:57.135 --> 00:13:59.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you commit to this
30-day, no-incident window,

00:13:59.705 --> 00:14:02.040 align:start size:88% position:13%
you just plan rotations
so there's no risk.

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.076
If they're not together,
we don't have a problem.

00:14:04.076 --> 00:14:06.078 align:start size:88% position:13%
If we just take fighting
off the table,

00:14:06.078 --> 00:14:07.679
then we change the way
we live with the dogs,

00:14:07.679 --> 00:14:09.148
they change their behavior.

00:14:09.148 --> 00:14:10.482 align:start size:91% position:9%
BRYANT: The hardest thing
for me moving forward

00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:13.685
is just staying consistent
every day for the next month

00:14:13.685 --> 00:14:15.487
to help solve the problem.

00:14:15.487 --> 00:14:18.490
MATT: I definitely would like to
see Eisenhower at the Zen yard.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.125
I'd love to see Truman there,

00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:22.828
it would probably be
mind-blowing for him.

00:14:22.828 --> 00:14:23.729
JUSTIN: Yeah.
BRYANT: Right.

00:14:23.729 --> 00:14:25.731 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: And to get Roosevelt
in there, too.

00:14:25.731 --> 00:14:27.299 align:start size:91% position:9%
JUSTIN: Oh, sounds a plan.
MATT: Alright.

00:14:27.299 --> 00:14:28.933
MATT: These dogs
desperately need

00:14:28.933 --> 00:14:30.936
supervised dog socialization.

00:14:30.936 --> 00:14:32.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
If we work to socialize them
at the Zen yard,

00:14:32.804 --> 00:14:34.606
we can control their environment

00:14:34.606 --> 00:14:35.841 line:0%
and then work to repair

00:14:35.841 --> 00:14:37.141 line:0%
their damaged relationship.

00:14:37.141 --> 00:14:38.109 line:0%
JUSTIN: Great, thanks so much.

00:14:38.109 --> 00:14:40.045 align:start size:88% position:13%
BRYANT: I appreciate it.
Thanks so much.

00:14:40.045 --> 00:14:42.014
MATT: Stay with the work.

00:14:43.348 --> 00:14:48.254
♪ ♪

00:14:48.254 --> 00:14:50.588 align:start size:91% position:9%
I really dig what happens
in the home sessions,

00:14:50.588 --> 00:14:51.957
but the other part of our work

00:14:51.957 --> 00:14:54.392 align:start size:97% position:3%
is what we do at the facility,
the Zen yard.

00:14:54.392 --> 00:14:56.661
You can come on in and
I'll show you the yards.

00:14:56.661 --> 00:14:59.865
My wife Brooklyn and I started
the Zen Dog about six years ago.

00:14:59.865 --> 00:15:02.067 align:start size:88% position:13%
The Zen Dog is a company
that believes

00:15:02.067 --> 00:15:04.636
that there are no bad dogs.

00:15:04.636 --> 00:15:06.404
(barking)

00:15:06.404 --> 00:15:07.873
Most of the dogs that
come to the Zen Dog

00:15:07.873 --> 00:15:11.010
are under socialized, they're
kicked out of other daycares,

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.378 align:start size:88% position:13%
they've had really awful
backstories

00:15:13.378 --> 00:15:15.380 align:start size:81% position:19%
or they're just
behaving naughtily.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.282
(laughs)

00:15:17.282 --> 00:15:19.451 align:start size:78% position:22%
I grew up watching
Mister Rogers.

00:15:19.451 --> 00:15:20.685
Come on, friend.

00:15:20.685 --> 00:15:23.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna show you the board
with all the advisories

00:15:23.354 --> 00:15:25.690
of the dogs who are
very, very dangerous.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.394
For example, BL5D.

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:29.494
Bite level five dog.

00:15:29.494 --> 00:15:31.529
That means that it's
a multiple puncture,

00:15:31.529 --> 00:15:34.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's so severe that
it requires hospitalization.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.634
Bite level six dog.

00:15:35.634 --> 00:15:38.570 align:start position:0%
This dog has killed another dog,
and they all show up here,

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:39.905
like the island
of lost children,

00:15:39.905 --> 00:15:43.275
and bit by bit, we find a way to
help them feel more comfortable

00:15:43.275 --> 00:15:44.543
and more confident.

00:15:44.543 --> 00:15:47.078
When I help the dog that
nobody else wanted to help

00:15:47.078 --> 00:15:49.314
and that dog changes for life,

00:15:49.314 --> 00:15:52.617 align:start size:91% position:9%
the payoff is as delicious
as ten puppies

00:15:52.617 --> 00:15:54.553
running around licking my face.

00:15:54.553 --> 00:15:55.921
(laughs)

00:15:57.389 --> 00:15:59.124 line:0%
(barking)

00:15:59.124 --> 00:16:01.126 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
Today Truman, Eisenhower
and Roosevelt

00:16:01.126 --> 00:16:04.729 line:0%
are coming into the Zen yard
for boarding and training.

00:16:04.729 --> 00:16:06.731
Justin and Bryant have not
been able to keep the dogs

00:16:06.731 --> 00:16:07.966
separate and peaceful,

00:16:07.966 --> 00:16:10.835
so we've decided to have them
