in bloodshed.

00:16:40.298 --> 00:16:43.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
Roosevelt is not happy
about his brother coming in.

00:16:43.368 --> 00:16:45.937 align:start position:0%
Eisenhower is clearly
threatening Roosevelt right now.

00:16:45.937 --> 00:16:49.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
STEF: Same thing on my end.
Hard stare, arms out.

00:16:49.274 --> 00:16:50.442
MATT: Yeah.

00:16:50.442 --> 00:16:53.712 align:start position:0%
STEF: Just stillness and staring
like, "I'm coming for you."

00:16:53.712 --> 00:16:54.780
MATT: Yeah.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.049
My sense is that if I let
Eisenhower out right now

00:16:57.049 --> 00:16:58.950 align:start size:88% position:13%
off-slip, that he would
attack Roosevelt.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.485
STEF: Agreed.
MATT: Yeah.

00:17:00.485 --> 00:17:04.022
MATT: Now we have a new and not
uncommon behavior from Roosevelt

00:17:04.022 --> 00:17:07.359 align:start position:0%
which is I'm just gonna lie here
but I'm gonna lie here

00:17:07.359 --> 00:17:09.994 align:start size:88% position:13%
in a place that actually
forces your hand.

00:17:09.994 --> 00:17:12.798
STEF: Yeah. I'm gonna lie here
and I'm gonna block the doorway.

00:17:12.798 --> 00:17:14.265
I'm gonna create
my own boundary.

00:17:14.265 --> 00:17:15.133
MATT: Yeah.

00:17:15.133 --> 00:17:16.234 align:start size:91% position:9%
STEF: And he's eyeing him
right now.

00:17:16.234 --> 00:17:17.202
MATT: Right.

00:17:17.202 --> 00:17:18.136
STEF: Oh, oh, growling.

00:17:18.136 --> 00:17:21.006
MATT: Yeah. Here we go.

00:17:21.006 --> 00:17:23.475 align:start size:88% position:13%
Okay, now the growling's
increasing.

00:17:23.475 --> 00:17:26.178
Because what's happening
is Roosevelt's not giving.

00:17:26.178 --> 00:17:28.447 align:start size:91% position:9%
This is real time
what happens in the home.

00:17:28.447 --> 00:17:29.681
(growling)

00:17:29.681 --> 00:17:30.916
MATT: There it is.
STEF: Scared me.

00:17:30.916 --> 00:17:32.184
MATT: Yeah, got me, too.

00:17:32.184 --> 00:17:34.987 align:start position:0% line:0%
So if we don't have them secure,
they're fighting right now.

00:17:34.987 --> 00:17:37.455 line:0%
It was really interesting that
Roosevelt made the first lunge

00:17:37.455 --> 00:17:39.691 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
even though Eisenhower
was the aggressor.

00:17:39.691 --> 00:17:41.860 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Even after Roosevelt laid down
essentially saying,

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:44.696 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
"Leave me alone, dude",
Eisenhower wouldn't back down.

00:17:44.696 --> 00:17:46.698
Roosevelt doesn't want
to initiate a fight.

00:17:46.698 --> 00:17:48.667 align:start size:97% position:3%
What Roosevelt has discovered
out of necessity

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:49.835
is he has to defend himself.

00:17:49.835 --> 00:17:50.635
STEF: Mm-hmm.

00:17:50.635 --> 00:17:52.704
MATT: Alright. Let's do a swap.

00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:54.606
Next I want to see what
Roosevelt's relationship

00:17:54.606 --> 00:17:56.508 line:0%
with Truman is like.

00:17:56.508 --> 00:17:57.976 line:0%
Okay, come on out.

00:17:57.976 --> 00:18:00.111 line:0%
These two aren't showing
the same type of aggression

00:18:00.111 --> 00:18:01.313
with one another right now,

00:18:01.313 --> 00:18:04.149
so it's a chance to get them
a little bit closer together

00:18:04.149 --> 00:18:05.383
and see what's going on.

00:18:05.383 --> 00:18:07.285
Let's go for a smell.

00:18:07.285 --> 00:18:09.988
STEF: It's your brother.

00:18:09.988 --> 00:18:11.122
MATT: Really?

00:18:11.122 --> 00:18:12.991
CAITLYN: Butt to butt.

00:18:12.991 --> 00:18:15.927 align:start position:0%
MATT: I mean, that's just weird.
That's not natural.

00:18:15.927 --> 00:18:20.899
Truman's grown up with this dog,
and they have no apparent desire

00:18:20.899 --> 00:18:23.468
to actually connect
with each other.

00:18:23.468 --> 00:18:26.471
And Truman keeps
making eye contact

00:18:26.471 --> 00:18:30.441 align:start size:81% position:19%
and Roosevelt keeps
turning away.

00:18:30.441 --> 00:18:32.243 align:start size:88% position:13%
What do you think about
going off-leash?

00:18:32.243 --> 00:18:33.278
STEF: I feel okay about it.

00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:36.181 align:start position:0%
MATT: Yeah, I do, too. Shall we?
STEF: Yeah.

00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:40.219 align:start size:84% position:16%
MATT: So the one thing
for us to watch for

00:18:40.219 --> 00:18:42.754
is anything that could
become resource guarding.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:46.758
Tss!

00:18:46.758 --> 00:18:48.660
Easy.

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.262
Yeah, there's something punky to
me about what's happening here.

00:18:51.262 --> 00:18:52.463
STEF: With Truman?

00:18:52.463 --> 00:18:54.265
MATT: Yeah, 'cause there's
a water bowl right there.

00:18:54.265 --> 00:18:56.301
This is not about you
drinking water, Truman,

00:18:56.301 --> 00:18:59.104
this is actually about who
is drinking the water bowl

00:18:59.104 --> 00:19:00.972 align:start size:81% position:19%
that you need to go
drink out of.

00:19:00.972 --> 00:19:02.974
And he's walking differently.

00:19:02.974 --> 00:19:04.709 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's a posturing about it,
right?

00:19:04.709 --> 00:19:07.112
Boom, boom, boom, boom.

00:19:07.112 --> 00:19:09.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
STEF: Like you are lingering
a little bit too long,

00:19:09.614 --> 00:19:11.316 align:start size:84% position:16%
kind of getting
on my nerves, Truman.

00:19:11.316 --> 00:19:12.550
MATT: Yeah.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
And Truman--Tss!
Hey, uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh.

00:19:20.158 --> 00:19:21.960 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: There's a posturing
about it, right?

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.528
Boom, boom, boom, boom.

00:19:23.528 --> 00:19:25.297
Hey, uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh.

00:19:25.297 --> 00:19:27.432 align:start size:91% position:9%
STEF: Punky, punky, punky.
MATT: Yeah.

00:19:27.432 --> 00:19:30.301 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
MATT: That is how you start
a fight with a dog

00:19:30.301 --> 00:19:31.770
that fights to defend itself,

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.439 align:start size:84% position:16%
that doesn't want
to be with you. Okay?

00:19:34.439 --> 00:19:37.709 align:start position:0% line:0%
STEF: And then he's cornered
himself, like I don't feel good.

00:19:37.709 --> 00:19:39.344 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
This feels
a little too familiar.

00:19:39.344 --> 00:19:40.212 line:0%
MATT: Yeah.

00:19:40.212 --> 00:19:41.246
STEF: Just look at
his whole demeanor.

00:19:41.246 --> 00:19:43.248
MATT: Yeah.

00:19:43.248 --> 00:19:45.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
STEF: His ears are back,
his head is low and hunched.

00:19:45.751 --> 00:19:47.719 align:start position:0%
MATT: And he's drooling. Right.
STEF: Lots of drool.

00:19:47.719 --> 00:19:49.588
STEF: And his eyes
are hanging heavy.

00:19:49.588 --> 00:19:51.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
MATT: He's just like,
this dog just shut him down.

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:52.991
Hi, sweetheart.

00:19:52.991 --> 00:19:54.358 align:start size:91% position:9%
STEF: And he keeps making
eye contact, though.

00:19:54.358 --> 00:19:55.660
MATT: Like, "Help me."
CAITLYN: With everybody.

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:56.628
MATT: Yeah, "Help me."

00:19:56.628 --> 00:19:59.097
Yeah. He is scared, and
he doesn't have somebody

00:19:59.097 --> 00:20:00.265
that's standing up for him.

00:20:00.265 --> 00:20:01.933 align:start size:75% position:25%
STEF: Yeah.
CAITLYN: Scared.

00:20:01.933 --> 00:20:04.403 align:start size:97% position:3%
CAITLYN: Makes me actually see
Roosevelt quite different,

00:20:04.403 --> 00:20:08.006 align:start position:0%
'cause I just saw him and
Eisenhower as these big bullies.

00:20:08.006 --> 00:20:10.308 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: And my heart really
hurts for this dog.

00:20:10.308 --> 00:20:13.111
During the home session,
the owners blame Roosevelt

00:20:13.111 --> 00:20:14.612
for starting most
of the violence,

00:20:14.612 --> 00:20:16.681
but he's actually
the victim here.

00:20:16.681 --> 00:20:18.483 align:start size:91% position:9%
Let's get him out of here
and secure

00:20:18.483 --> 00:20:21.085 align:start size:88% position:13%
and let's go right
into Eisenhower/Truman.

00:20:21.085 --> 00:20:22.820
STEF: I got Rosie.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.957 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: Truman, you can have
the yard, buddy.

00:20:25.957 --> 00:20:27.058
STEF: Coming out.

00:20:27.058 --> 00:20:30.462 line:0%
Come on, Eisenhower. Let's go.

00:20:30.462 --> 00:20:31.730
So different.

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.766
MATT: Right, and he doesn't come
over and say hi to his brother.

00:20:34.766 --> 00:20:36.501 align:start size:91% position:9%
CAITLYN: And Truman's head
is lower.

00:20:36.501 --> 00:20:37.469
MATT: Yeah.

00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:39.537 align:start size:91% position:9%
CAITLYN: He has that more
like, I'm afraid,

00:20:39.537 --> 00:20:41.840
I don't want to be in here.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:44.142 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: Now look, Truman...
CAITLYN: Wants to go.

00:20:44.142 --> 00:20:46.044 align:start size:88% position:13%
MATT: Yeah, okay,
let's pause right there.

00:20:46.044 --> 00:20:49.381 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's how that looked to me.
Yeah. Truman wants out.

00:20:49.381 --> 00:20:50.214 align:start size:84% position:16%
CAITLYN: He just wants
to get out.

00:20:50.214 --> 00:20:51.483 align:start size:88% position:13%
STEF: And all he wanted
to do is stay in

00:20:51.483 --> 00:20:52.517 align:start size:78% position:22%
and punk Roosevelt
the whole time.

00:20:52.517 --> 00:20:53.317
MATT: Right.

00:20:53.317 --> 00:20:54.552
Truman became a different dog

00:20:54.552 --> 00:20:56.354
while he was alone
with Eisenhower.

00:20:56.354 --> 00:20:59.657 align:start size:91% position:9%
He totally shut down
and was overrun with fear.

00:20:59.657 --> 00:21:02.360 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's clear Eisenhower's on
the top of this social ladder.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:05.697
So we've got the same cycle of
violence happening in the house,

00:21:05.697 --> 00:21:09.334
because you've got this one
who started it on Roosevelt

00:21:09.334 --> 00:21:11.702 align:start size:91% position:9%
and Roosevelt began
to have to defend himself.

00:21:11.702 --> 00:21:13.572
Then you get Truman who says,

00:21:13.572 --> 00:21:16.475 align:start position:0%
"Oh, this is how this operates,
we punk Roosevelt."

00:21:16.475 --> 00:21:19.777
He's learning violence
from Eisenhower for sure.

00:21:19.777 --> 00:21:22.580 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's not just a pecking order,
it's the bitch ladder.

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:25.750
But a good parent does
not allow their dogs

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:29.221 align:start size:97% position:3%
to have these kinds of
relationships without healing.

00:21:29.221 --> 00:21:32.157 align:start position:0%
Moving forward, we need to
socialize these dogs separately.

00:21:32.157 --> 00:21:34.358 line:0%
They need to realize that
they can have relationships

00:21:34.358 --> 00:21:36.894 line:0%
with other dogs that aren't
built on fear and aggression,

00:21:36.894 --> 00:21:38.863
but can be healthy and secure.

00:21:38.863 --> 00:21:40.132
This didn't happen overnight,

00:21:40.132 --> 00:21:41.733 align:start size:84% position:16%
so it's not gonna get
fixed overnight.

00:21:41.733 --> 00:21:43.801 align:start size:78% position:22%
We are way further
down the weeds

00:21:43.801 --> 00:21:44.936
than I thought we were gonna be

00:21:44.936 --> 00:21:46.871
in terms of their
dog socialization,

00:21:46.871 --> 00:21:48.139
but it's all workable.

00:21:48.139 --> 00:21:50.775
So I know there's hope here.

00:21:50.775 --> 00:21:53.745
(barking)

00:21:53.745 --> 00:21:55.514 align:start size:91% position:9%
The way we work with dogs
is different

00:21:55.514 --> 00:21:59.517 align:start size:97% position:3%
in that we don't use any
conventional training methods.

00:21:59.517 --> 00:22:01.419
STEF: Coming in with Pax.

00:22:01.419 --> 00:22:03.822 line:0%
MATT: We're not using treats,
shock collars, choke chains,

00:22:03.822 --> 00:22:06.658 line:0%
prong collars, commands.

00:22:06.658 --> 00:22:08.159 align:start size:84% position:16%
Everything is designed
for the dog

00:22:08.159 --> 00:22:09.427
to be able to think for itself,

00:22:09.427 --> 00:22:10.996 align:start size:81% position:19%
'cause a dog that
can think for itself

00:22:10.996 --> 00:22:12.964
is not gonna be reactive.

00:22:12.964 --> 00:22:16.334 align:start size:84% position:16%
This dog has got
some dangerous issues.

00:22:16.334 --> 00:22:20.205 align:start size:97% position:3%
He was in blackout aggression
in the home.

00:22:20.205 --> 00:22:22.173
(barking)

00:22:22.173 --> 00:22:23.174
In the home visit,

00:22:23.174 --> 00:22:25.543
we couldn't even get Pax
safely out of the crate.

00:22:25.543 --> 00:22:27.178
Today he's letting
Stef handle him,

00:22:27.178 --> 00:22:29.614 align:start size:88% position:13%
so I want to see if Pax
can remain calm

00:22:29.614 --> 00:22:31.649 align:start size:88% position:13%
while being in the yard
with another dog.

00:22:31.649 --> 00:22:32.950
Coming out with Mina.

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:35.253
Just because Pax lives
with another dog, Emma,

00:22:35.253 --> 00:22:37.355 align:start size:91% position:9%
doesn't mean that he knows
how to behave with dogs

00:22:37.355 --> 00:22:39.056
he doesn't know
out in the world.

00:22:39.056 --> 00:22:42.227
Yeah, he certainly seems intent.

00:22:42.227 --> 00:22:44.262 align:start size:91% position:9%
What's different about
what we do in the facility

00:22:44.262 --> 00:22:46.164
is we have dogs
to help us teach,

00:22:46.164 --> 00:22:48.333
dogs get to be with dogs
that are good role models.

00:22:48.333 --> 00:22:49.767
If they can be trustworthy,

00:22:49.767 --> 00:22:53.304
it's fundamental to their
experience in being alive

00:22:53.304 --> 00:22:55.507
that they get to be a dog
and know what that's like.

00:22:55.507 --> 00:22:58.176 align:start size:78% position:22%
STEF: So why don't
we give Pax...

00:22:58.176 --> 00:22:59.477 align:start size:78% position:22%
MATT: First smell?
STEF: Mm-hmm.

00:22:59.477 --> 00:23:00.645
MATT: Come here, sugar plum.

00:23:00.645 --> 00:23:03.147 align:start position:0%
Smelling another dog is
the equivalent of saying hello.

00:23:03.147 --> 00:23:06.017
Pax is gonna smell you, okay?

00:23:06.017 --> 00:23:07.085
STEF: Uh-uh.

00:23:07.085 --> 00:23:09.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
MATT: I'm not gonna
let you get hurt. I promise.

00:23:12.123 --> 00:23:15.394
His breathing picks up,
his eyes are bugging out.

00:23:17.128 --> 00:23:19.430 align:start size:97% position:3%
STEF: Just is rude and pushy.
MATT: Yeah.

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:21.833 align:start size:97% position:3%
STEF: And like, I don't really
know what I'm doing either.

00:23:21.833 --> 00:23:24.236
MATT: Under-socialized.

00:23:24.236 --> 00:23:26.137
STEF: Come on.

00:23:26.137 --> 00:23:29.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
MATT: It's interesting that
I got a few eyes there.

00:23:29.307 --> 00:23:30.474
STEF: Let's go ahead
and get the hose out

00:23:30.474 --> 00:23:33.211
just in case Pax does
decide to go after you.

00:23:33.211 --> 00:23:34.612 align:start size:78% position:22%
MATT: A hose is
a great inhibitor.

00:23:34.612 --> 00:23:36.981 align:start size:91% position:9%
We spray the hose
so that it's near the dog.

00:23:36.981 --> 00:23:38.149
We just want the dog to know

00:23:38.149 --> 00:23:41.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
that this is part
of the communication.

00:23:41.018 --> 00:23:42.387
He's got eyes on me, I can tell.

00:23:42.387 --> 00:23:43.654 align:start size:81% position:19%
STEF: He's terrified
of the hose.

00:23:43.654 --> 00:23:45.990
You bring it out and he almost
shuts down and doesn't recover.

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:48.126 align:start size:91% position:9%
And there he goes.
He just saw you go for it.

00:23:48.126 --> 00:23:49.927
MATT: And now he wants
to get the muzzle off

00:23:49.927 --> 00:23:52.197
now that he sees me as a threat.

00:23:52.197 --> 00:23:53.331
STEF: Mm-hmm.

00:23:53.331 --> 00:23:55.533 align:start size:84% position:16%
MATT: He seems
particularly keyed up.

00:23:55.533 --> 00:23:58.303
I've got no hose, okay,
I'm sorry you got scared.

00:23:58.303 --> 00:23:59.504
Didn't mean to scare you.

00:23:59.504 --> 00:24:01.205
STEF: That's how sensitive
Pax is to his fear triggers.

00:24:01.205 --> 00:24:03.340 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: There's a stiffness
about him

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:06.011
that usually precedes an attack.

00:24:06.011 --> 00:24:08.313
This dog is a powder keg.

00:24:08.313 --> 00:24:11.149 align:start size:84% position:16%
There we go,
let's let this happen.

00:24:11.149 --> 00:24:14.085
Okay? Okay?

00:24:15.219 --> 00:24:17.189
Okay?

00:24:17.189 --> 00:24:18.690
Take the leash.

00:24:18.690 --> 00:24:20.291
STEF: He just goes
right for the face.

00:24:20.291 --> 00:24:22.760
Right alongside the neck, too.

00:24:22.760 --> 00:24:23.662
MATT: Shady.

00:24:23.662 --> 00:24:25.963
STEF: It's so needy
and so desperate.

00:24:25.963 --> 00:24:27.332
MATT: And creepy.

00:24:27.332 --> 00:24:29.467 align:start size:84% position:16%
Pax does not know
how to deal with fear.

00:24:29.467 --> 00:24:31.836
Pax needs to learn
how to calm himself.

00:24:31.836 --> 00:24:33.404
That's gonna require detachment

00:24:33.404 --> 00:24:35.173 align:start size:91% position:9%
and appropriate affection
at home

00:24:35.173 --> 00:24:37.542 align:start size:91% position:9%
and intense socialization
here at the Zen yard.

00:24:37.542 --> 00:24:42.146
The kid doesn't know
he's not a bad dog.

00:24:42.146 --> 00:24:47.152
♪ ♪

00:24:47.152 --> 00:24:49.787 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
MATT: Come on, kiddo.
STEF: Let's go.

00:24:49.787 --> 00:24:52.590 line:0%
MATT: Today we're gonna start
socialization work with Truman.

00:24:52.590 --> 00:24:54.392 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
We have a surprise party
planned for you.

00:24:54.392 --> 00:24:55.460
STEF: Let's go, bud.

00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:57.261 align:start position:0%
MATT: This is a dog who's afraid
of almost everything,

00:24:57.261 --> 00:24:59.798
and on top of that he's been
learning some very bad habits

00:24:59.798 --> 00:25:01.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
from his older brother
Eisenhower

00:25:01.266 --> 00:25:03.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
about how to interact
with other dogs.

00:25:03.701 --> 00:25:06.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
STEF: Phew.
He is just a hot mess.

00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:08.807
Come on, bud. Good boy.

00:25:08.807 --> 00:25:10.174 align:start size:81% position:19%
MATT: We're gonna
start him with Huck,

00:25:10.174 --> 00:25:13.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of my favorites and
one of our most secure dogs.

00:25:13.645 --> 00:25:16.181
I'm surprised that he's
this frightened of Huck.

00:25:16.181 --> 00:25:18.916 align:start size:84% position:16%
STEF: It's like
a stubbornness and...

00:25:18.916 --> 00:25:19.718
MATT: Yeah.

00:25:19.718 --> 00:25:21.052 align:start size:81% position:19%
STEF: He disconnects
immediately.

00:25:21.052 --> 00:25:22.453
MATT: Good boy. Yeah.

00:25:22.453 --> 00:25:23.721
STEF: And he goes back
into like his shell.

00:25:23.721 --> 00:25:25.689
MATT: Good boy, Truman.

00:25:25.689 --> 00:25:27.959
What's happening here
is I'm not pulling,

00:25:27.959 --> 00:25:32.030 align:start size:97% position:3%
but when there's a sliver
of release, which I can feel,

00:25:32.030 --> 00:25:34.498 align:start size:88% position:13%
good boy, Truman,
by not counter pulling,

00:25:34.498 --> 00:25:36.267 align:start size:88% position:13%
when there's a good boy,
like that.

00:25:36.267 --> 00:25:38.670
That's it right there.

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:40.071
Gorgeous.

00:25:40.071 --> 00:25:43.008
And so in spite of himself, he
actually had a dog experience.

00:25:43.008 --> 00:25:43.875
STEF: Mm-hmm.

00:25:43.875 --> 00:25:45.776
MATT: And if I had
let him dictate it,

00:25:45.776 --> 00:25:47.145
he would have been
back in the crate,

00:25:47.145 --> 00:25:48.312
and we would have
written this off

00:25:48.312 --> 00:25:49.847
and said it's not gonna work.

00:25:49.847 --> 00:25:51.616
And not only did he just do it,

00:25:51.616 --> 00:25:54.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
he did it without us having
to tell him what to do.

00:25:54.285 --> 00:25:55.953
Let's see if Huck can smell you.

00:25:55.953 --> 00:25:57.154 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm just gonna hang
onto you here,

00:25:57.154 --> 00:25:59.424 align:start size:91% position:9%
and Huck's gonna come over
and smell you, okay?

00:25:59.424 --> 00:26:01.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I don't have any tension
on my hand,

00:26:01.225 --> 00:26:02.594
there's no tension on the leash.

00:26:02.594 --> 00:26:04.329
Good boy, Huck.

00:26:04.329 --> 00:26:05.196
STEF: Good boy, bud.

00:26:05.196 --> 00:26:06.865 align:start size:81% position:19%
MATT: He's breathing
pretty heavy,

00:26:06.865 --> 00:26:09.701
but that was Huck and
nothing happened, huh?

00:26:09.701 --> 00:26:11.235 align:start size:91% position:9%
Now we want to up the ante
a little bit

00:26:11.235 --> 00:26:12.970
by bringing in Licorice.

00:26:12.970 --> 00:26:15.406
He's still a secure dog,
but a bit more high energy,

00:26:15.406 --> 00:26:18.209 align:start size:91% position:9%
so I want to see if Truman
can still stay calm.

00:26:18.209 --> 00:26:19.176
Come here, kiddo.

00:26:19.176 --> 00:26:21.779
Do you want to smell Licorice?

00:26:21.779 --> 00:26:24.215 align:start position:0%
I'm telling you, I asked him if
he wanted to smell Licorice

00:26:24.215 --> 00:26:25.817
and he started moving.

00:26:25.817 --> 00:26:26.951
Okay, there's the lip.

00:26:26.951 --> 00:26:28.386
(barking)

00:26:33.391 --> 00:26:36.627 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
MATT: Come here, kiddo.
Do you want to smell Licorice?

00:26:36.627 --> 00:26:37.895
Okay, there's the lip.

00:26:37.895 --> 00:26:39.797
There is it. Yeah.

00:26:39.797 --> 00:26:42.433
I saw lip and I felt growl.

00:26:42.433 --> 00:26:45.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
Licorice was a bit too much
for Truman to handle.

00:26:45.003 --> 00:26:46.070
Licorice got in his space

00:26:46.070 --> 00:26:49.273 align:start position:0%
and gave him a few playful barks
and Truman shut down.

00:26:49.273 --> 00:26:50.474
Truman's pulling right now,

00:26:50.474 --> 00:26:53.244 align:start position:0%
'cause he doesn't want anything
to do with being Truman.

00:26:53.244 --> 00:26:55.412 align:start size:91% position:9%
He wants "The Truman Show"
canceled,

00:26:55.412 --> 00:26:58.716
and he wants to get out of here
and go back to being nothing.

00:26:58.716 --> 00:27:00.485
STEF: There's just an overall

00:27:00.485 --> 00:27:03.421
blanket of nerves
and insecurity.

00:27:03.421 --> 00:27:06.023
MATT: We're gonna continue
intense dog socialization

00:27:06.023 --> 00:27:08.359
to help Truman feel more
comfortable in his own skin

00:27:08.359 --> 00:27:10.428
and eventually with
his own brothers.

00:27:10.428 --> 00:27:11.562
Come on, my love bug.

00:27:11.562 --> 00:27:12.997
STEF: Coming out.

00:27:12.997 --> 00:27:19.037
♪ ♪

00:27:19.037 --> 00:27:21.939
(barking)

00:27:21.939 --> 00:27:23.341
MATT: Every once
in a great while,

00:27:23.341 --> 00:27:26.578 line:0%
the Zen Dog will foster a dog;
dogs that have maimed humans,

00:27:26.578 --> 00:27:28.379 align:start size:78% position:22%
dogs that have
killed other dogs.

00:27:28.379 --> 00:27:30.882
We commit to getting them
the help that they need

00:27:30.882 --> 00:27:35.686
so that they can get adopted
and put in a good forever home.

00:27:35.686 --> 00:27:37.021 align:start size:88% position:13%
Alright, we're gonna go
meet Lincoln.

00:27:37.021 --> 00:27:40.224 align:start position:0%
I say that there are no
bad dogs, 'cause I was that dog.

00:27:40.224 --> 00:27:44.662
When I started this whole
journey, I was detoxing.

00:27:44.662 --> 00:27:46.364
(barking)

00:27:46.364 --> 00:27:48.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hi, hi, hi, hi, hi.
Here, I'll take my hat off.

00:27:48.967 --> 00:27:50.501
(barking)

00:27:50.501 --> 00:27:52.369 align:start size:81% position:19%
I grew up making
all kinds of choices

00:27:52.369 --> 00:27:55.239
that put my life and other
people's lives in danger.

00:27:55.239 --> 00:27:57.008
I was given a second chance,

00:27:57.008 --> 00:28:01.379 align:start position:0%
so I look at the dogs as a
reflection of my own experience.

00:28:01.379 --> 00:28:05.283
(barking)

00:28:05.283 --> 00:28:08.352 align:start size:88% position:13%
So this is pretty normal
for he and I.

00:28:08.352 --> 00:28:11.089
The story goes that I look like
somebody that he was adopted

00:28:11.089 --> 00:28:14.091 align:start position:0%
and returned by, and apparently
was never the same dog

00:28:14.091 --> 00:28:15.660
after he was returned.

00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:17.428 align:start size:88% position:13%
I have a real soft spot
for Lincoln.

00:28:17.428 --> 00:28:20.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's exactly the kind of dog
that's a last chance dog

00:28:20.698 --> 00:28:22.600
that's been misunderstood

00:28:22.600 --> 00:28:25.969
and a dog that just needs
an opportunity to learn

00:28:25.969 --> 00:28:28.973
how to relate with human beings.

00:28:28.973 --> 00:28:31.642 align:start size:97% position:3%
You can see his trust in Amy;
immediately he softens.

00:28:31.642 --> 00:28:34.979
AMY: Hi. Hi. Yeah.

00:28:34.979 --> 00:28:35.913
MATT: See?

00:28:35.913 --> 00:28:37.682
You stay there and
I'm gonna step in

00:28:37.682 --> 00:28:39.617
and let's see what happens.

00:28:41.119 --> 00:28:42.887
(barking)

00:28:42.887 --> 00:28:43.921
(growling)

00:28:43.921 --> 00:28:45.823
It's okay. It's just me.

00:28:45.823 --> 00:28:47.725 align:start size:84% position:16%
Especially with a dog
this reactive,

00:28:47.725 --> 00:28:50.261
detachment is the key
to everything we do.

00:28:50.261 --> 00:28:52.563 align:start size:88% position:13%
If I remain detached
and I don't provoke him,

00:28:52.563 --> 00:28:55.200
he will learn to
calm himself down.

00:28:56.634 --> 00:28:58.869
Good boy, Lincoln.

00:28:58.869 --> 00:29:02.607
You can hear the pause in there.

00:29:02.607 --> 00:29:05.910 align:start position:0%
You could see how that made
space for his energy to change.

00:29:05.910 --> 00:29:08.879
If we change energy, we change
behavior, which is what he did.

00:29:08.879 --> 00:29:11.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
There, you see it?
There's the downshift.

00:29:11.949 --> 00:29:16.087 align:start size:81% position:19%
Drops his head,
the barking changes.

00:29:16.087 --> 00:29:18.723
The body goes from that
tense state that he's in

00:29:18.723 --> 00:29:20.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now there's a little bit
of movement.

00:29:20.290 --> 00:29:22.026
There we go, and he's closer.

00:29:22.026 --> 00:29:24.261 align:start position:0%
That's the significance of what
happened for Lincoln today;

00:29:24.261 --> 00:29:26.664
he got to face his fear
and work through it.

00:29:26.664 --> 00:29:28.499 align:start size:81% position:19%
If he can work
through it with me,

00:29:28.499 --> 00:29:30.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
he can work through it
with anybody else.

00:29:30.435 --> 00:29:31.936
Good boy.

00:29:31.936 --> 00:29:35.740
You big, beautiful,
bowling ball-headed,

00:29:35.740 --> 00:29:38.843 align:start size:91% position:9%
you're like a big walking
Thanksgiving turkey.

00:29:41.779 --> 00:29:46.718
♪ ♪

00:29:46.718 --> 00:29:49.320
(phone ringing)

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:51.222 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> RAYHAN: Hello?</i>
 MATT: Hey, it's Matt Beisner.

00:29:51.222 --> 00:29:52.490 align:start size:81% position:19%
MATT: Today, I want
to get a sense

00:29:52.490 --> 00:29:53.825
for how Pax is progressing.

00:29:53.825 --> 00:29:58.863
I wanted to meet with the three
of you and do some walking work.

00:29:58.863 --> 00:30:00.164
STEF: Might say hello.

00:30:00.164 --> 00:30:02.333 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
MATT: We've been working with
Pax for the last few days

00:30:02.333 --> 00:30:04.601
through some intense
socialization training.

00:30:04.601 --> 00:30:05.937
STEF: You're doing great, Mina.

00:30:05.937 --> 00:30:08.272 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: Since Pax went home,
his owners, Riddhi and Rayhan,

00:30:08.272 --> 00:30:09.607
have been practicing detachment,

00:30:09.607 --> 00:30:12.409 align:start size:97% position:3%
making sure they only give Pax
affection when he's calm.

00:30:12.409 --> 00:30:15.579 align:start size:97% position:3%
That way, they don't reinforce
his anxiety and aggression.

00:30:15.579 --> 00:30:17.681
RIDDHI: Good boy, Pax.

00:30:17.681 --> 00:30:19.283 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: I'll be a little bit
further up the path,

00:30:19.283 --> 00:30:21.519
and I just want to do
one pass by first,

00:30:21.519 --> 00:30:24.021 align:start size:97% position:3%
because I just want to see
where Pax is at with me, okay?

00:30:24.021 --> 00:30:25.055
<i> RAYHAN: Okay, sounds good.</i>

00:30:25.055 --> 00:30:25.956
MATT: Okay, cool.

00:30:25.956 --> 00:30:27.825 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm wearing dark clothes
and I do have a hat,

00:30:27.825 --> 00:30:30.495
so I know I'm already
a walking trigger.

00:30:30.495 --> 00:30:32.129 line:0%
So I'm just gonna walk by

00:30:32.129 --> 00:30:35.399 line:0%
and we're not gonna pay
each other any attention.

00:30:35.399 --> 00:30:37.401
♪ ♪

00:30:37.401 --> 00:30:43.141
♪ ♪

00:30:46.711 --> 00:30:48.679 align:start size:78% position:22%
Wow, he's doing
a really nice job.

00:30:48.679 --> 00:30:51.048 align:start size:88% position:13%
Your leash handling
looks great, by the way.

00:30:51.048 --> 00:30:53.117
You look calm and clear,

00:30:53.117 --> 00:30:56.954 align:start size:91% position:9%
and I didn't see a change
in him at all.

00:30:56.954 --> 00:30:58.155
RIDDHI: No, he just walked by.

00:30:58.155 --> 00:30:59.324
MATT: Yeah.
RIDDHI: Yeah.

00:30:59.324 --> 00:31:00.491
MATT: Excellent.

00:31:00.491 --> 00:31:03.528
So why don't the three
of you start walking?

00:31:06.797 --> 00:31:08.900 align:start size:84% position:16%
And just pay attention
really to anything,

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:10.934 align:start size:88% position:13%
yeah, there he is
shaking off the stress.

00:31:10.934 --> 00:31:14.739
Anything that you notice, see
there's a little pull in there.

00:31:16.140 --> 00:31:17.975 line:0%
MATT: Oh, yeah, to get
the muzzle off, right?

00:31:17.975 --> 00:31:18.809
RAYHAN: Yeah.
RIDDHI: Yeah.

00:31:18.809 --> 00:31:20.044
MATT: Yeah, okay.

00:31:20.044 --> 00:31:22.480 align:start size:81% position:19%
Well, I know
it's a big ask, Pax,

00:31:22.480 --> 00:31:25.015 align:start size:88% position:13%
I know I just dropped in
on a walk with you.

00:31:25.015 --> 00:31:27.018
Let's switch, let's turn around.

00:31:27.018 --> 00:31:30.021 align:start size:97% position:3%
Rayhan, you take him
and we're gonna walk together.

00:31:30.021 --> 00:31:31.489 align:start size:69% position:31%
(barking)
RAYHAN: Pax!

00:31:38.229 --> 00:31:41.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
MATT: So why don't the three
of you start walking?

00:31:41.332 --> 00:31:44.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today I really want to focus
on Pax's triggers.

00:31:44.568 --> 00:31:46.270
Let's switch, let's turn around.

00:31:46.270 --> 00:31:49.173
Rayhan, you take him and
we're gonna walk together.

00:31:49.173 --> 00:31:53.010 align:start size:97% position:3%
As soon as I joined the walk,
Pax is cagey.

00:31:53.010 --> 00:31:54.178
We're gonna do it anyway, kiddo.

00:31:54.178 --> 00:31:55.847 align:start size:84% position:16%
I just want to see you
walk with me.

00:31:55.847 --> 00:31:57.215
When he encounters stress,

00:31:57.215 --> 00:32:02.419 align:start position:0%
he needs to learn to calm
himself instead of lashing out.

00:32:02.419 --> 00:32:03.888 align:start position:0%
RIDDHI: You're doing good, Pax,
doing good.

00:32:03.888 --> 00:32:06.490
MATT: We'll walk together.

00:32:06.490 --> 00:32:08.926
There we go.

00:32:08.926 --> 00:32:12.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
That a boy, Pax.
Good boy, Pax. I know.

00:32:12.163 --> 00:32:14.832 align:start size:97% position:3%
You don't have to like it,
but you're doing great, buddy.

00:32:14.832 --> 00:32:17.434 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is subtle,
but it's a big moment for Pax.

00:32:17.434 --> 00:32:19.037
He stayed connected with Rayhan,

00:32:19.037 --> 00:32:22.206 align:start size:97% position:3%
he kept moving and
he was able to keep his cool.

00:32:22.206 --> 00:32:24.708 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
What I saw today was
promising in a lot of ways.

00:32:24.708 --> 00:32:25.943 line:0%
It definitely stood out to me

00:32:25.943 --> 00:32:29.646 align:start position:0%
that Pax was able to walk by me
without reacting.

00:32:29.646 --> 00:32:31.883
When he did start to react...

00:32:31.883 --> 00:32:33.517 align:start size:69% position:31%
(barking)
RAYHAN: Pax!

00:32:33.517 --> 00:32:35.186
MATT: His reactions
were not as intense.

00:32:35.186 --> 00:32:38.089 align:start size:84% position:16%
He didn't stay hot
as long as he used to.

00:32:38.089 --> 00:32:39.957 align:start size:81% position:19%
He actually was able
to let it go,

00:32:39.957 --> 00:32:43.161
as evidenced by the fact
that after all of that,

00:32:43.161 --> 00:32:47.598
we end up walking together
and Pax doesn't come at me.

00:32:47.598 --> 00:32:50.501
Good boy, Pax. Good boy, buddy.

00:32:50.501 --> 00:32:53.237 align:start size:81% position:19%
We'll talk about
what we can do next.

00:32:53.237 --> 00:32:55.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
Pax has to continue
coming to the Zen yard

00:32:55.506 --> 00:32:58.176
for regular dog and
human socialization,

00:32:58.176 --> 00:33:01.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
otherwise he risks backsliding
into dangerous behavior.

00:33:01.879 --> 00:33:06.951
♪ ♪

00:33:06.951 --> 00:33:08.986 line:0%
Coming in with Eisenhower.

00:33:08.986 --> 00:33:12.590 line:0%
Eisenhower is the toxic alpha
of this bulldog pack at home,

00:33:12.590 --> 00:33:13.791
and he deals with the stress

00:33:13.791 --> 00:33:16.493
by bullying and fighting
like most human bullies.

00:33:16.493 --> 00:33:17.595
Underneath it all,

00:33:17.595 --> 00:33:20.465
he's literally drowning
in insecurity and fear.

00:33:20.465 --> 00:33:22.232
STEF: Oh, buddy.

00:33:22.232 --> 00:33:25.369 align:start position:0%
MATT: This dog is brokenhearted
and terrified.

00:33:25.369 --> 00:33:26.837 line:0%
STEF: Come on, Nama.

00:33:26.837 --> 00:33:29.106 line:0%
MATT: I'm gonna bring in
my delicious dog, Nama.

00:33:29.106 --> 00:33:30.807 line:0%
She's secure in her rank,

00:33:30.807 --> 00:33:32.176
and she's gonna show Eisenhower

00:33:32.176 --> 00:33:34.244 align:start size:81% position:19%
the kind of dog
that he can become.

00:33:34.244 --> 00:33:35.813
We're gonna have you meet Nama.

00:33:35.813 --> 00:33:37.448
You just haven't been
taught social manners,

00:33:37.448 --> 00:33:40.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we're gonna show you
in our own clunky human way

00:33:40.484 --> 00:33:42.252
what that's like.

00:33:42.252 --> 00:33:44.388
We're gonna come around this way

00:33:44.388 --> 00:33:47.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
and let's come right in here
and see what's there.

00:33:47.691 --> 00:33:48.693
There we go.

00:33:48.693 --> 00:33:50.061
Good boy.

00:33:50.061 --> 00:33:51.828
God boy, Eisen.

00:33:51.828 --> 00:33:54.399
And he looks at me like,
"Is that how I do it?"

00:33:54.399 --> 00:33:56.634 align:start size:97% position:3%
He smelled it like he'd never
had an opportunity

00:33:56.634 --> 00:33:58.669 align:start size:78% position:22%
to do that before.
Even this.

00:33:58.669 --> 00:34:02.039
I think you're actually gonna
try and throw a little--boom.

00:34:02.039 --> 00:34:03.240
You see how unassuming,

00:34:03.240 --> 00:34:05.609 align:start position:0%
and look it, he checks with Stef
to see if that's okay.

00:34:05.609 --> 00:34:07.010
STEF: That's great, bud.

00:34:07.010 --> 00:34:08.946
MATT: Right? You do not
want to be a monster.

00:34:08.946 --> 00:34:11.382
Smelling Nama's a really
big deal for Eisenhower,

00:34:11.382 --> 00:34:13.551 align:start position:0%
and he couldn't have done better
for where he's at.

00:34:13.551 --> 00:34:14.785 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm gonna hang on to you
right here,

00:34:14.785 --> 00:34:16.720
'cause Nama wants to smell you.

00:34:16.720 --> 00:34:19.490 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now I want to have Eisenhower
get smelled by Nama,

00:34:19.490 --> 00:34:22.660 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is gonna require
a lot more trust on his part.

00:34:24.061 --> 00:34:26.364
There we go. There's the fear.

00:34:26.364 --> 00:34:28.799 align:start position:0%
(growling)
Okay, so now we've got growling.

00:34:28.799 --> 00:34:31.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
In his experience,
it's actually not safe

00:34:31.401 --> 00:34:34.038 align:start size:88% position:13%
to have somebody come up
from behind you.

00:34:34.038 --> 00:34:36.940
We need to keep working
on the social experience

00:34:36.940 --> 00:34:39.243 align:start size:88% position:13%
for Eisenhower,
help him get to a place

00:34:39.243 --> 00:34:41.545 align:start size:81% position:19%
where he feels
secure and trusting,

00:34:41.545 --> 00:34:44.382 align:start position:0%
and then he's got a shot at
making things work in the home.

00:34:44.382 --> 00:34:46.317
Coming out with Ike.

00:34:48.785 --> 00:34:51.822 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
STEF: Coming in with Pax.
(barking)

00:34:51.822 --> 00:34:54.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
MATT: Pax has been coming in
for regular day play,

00:34:54.224 --> 00:34:55.760
and he's making good progress.

00:34:55.760 --> 00:34:56.827
STEF: Good boy.

00:34:56.827 --> 00:34:59.496 align:start size:88% position:13%
Hi, bud.
Thanks for sitting down.

00:34:59.496 --> 00:35:01.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
MATT: Stef has been able
to work with him off-muzzle,

00:35:01.498 --> 00:35:03.634
which shows how far he's come.

00:35:03.634 --> 00:35:07.037
Remarkable how different
already in holding with you

00:35:07.037 --> 00:35:09.006 align:start size:84% position:16%
from where we left off
in the home.

00:35:09.006 --> 00:35:11.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today I'm hoping he'll walk
with me off-muzzle.

00:35:15.246 --> 00:35:16.881 align:start size:97% position:3%
STEF: Why don't you walk next
to me for a little while?

00:35:16.881 --> 00:35:19.450
MATT: Okay. Hi, Pax.

00:35:19.450 --> 00:35:21.018
I see you.

00:35:21.018 --> 00:35:22.920
I see you see me.

00:35:22.920 --> 00:35:26.691
Since Pax trusts Stef, I'm gonna
try and draft off of that energy

00:35:26.691 --> 00:35:32.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
and hopefully we can transfer
his trust in her to me.

00:35:32.863 --> 00:35:34.832 align:start size:88% position:13%
No, my friend. Come on.
(clicks tongue)

00:35:34.832 --> 00:35:36.700
(bark)

00:35:36.700 --> 00:35:40.003
I'll take it. Yeah. Hi.

00:35:40.003 --> 00:35:41.505 align:start size:75% position:25%
(clicks tongue)
Let's walk.

00:35:41.505 --> 00:35:43.140
Up, up, up, let's walk.

00:35:43.140 --> 00:35:45.209 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: That a boy. There we go.
STEF: Good.

00:35:45.209 --> 00:35:47.445 align:start size:88% position:13%
MATT: There we go.
We're gonna keep moving.

00:35:47.445 --> 00:35:49.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want him to get in
movement and rhythm with me.

00:35:49.981 --> 00:35:51.181
Good boy, Pax.

00:35:51.181 --> 00:35:54.918
I know that the momentum is
gonna help him stay unstuck.

00:35:54.918 --> 00:35:57.087
There we go, we're gonna
take this corner, too.

00:35:57.087 --> 00:35:58.622 align:start size:88% position:13%
The momentum of walking
helps dogs

00:35:58.622 --> 00:36:00.758
move through their
anxiety and fear.

00:36:00.758 --> 00:36:03.628
That's why movement is such
a big part of our training.

00:36:05.863 --> 00:36:06.964
STEF: Good boy.

00:36:06.964 --> 00:36:08.299
MATT: Good boy, Pax.

00:36:08.299 --> 00:36:10.334
This feels like a big
breakthrough for Pax.

00:36:10.334 --> 00:36:12.103
It's amazing to me
how far he's come,

00:36:12.103 --> 00:36:13.837 align:start size:78% position:22%
but his owners
need to understand

00:36:13.837 --> 00:36:15.606
there is no room for error.

00:36:15.606 --> 00:36:18.408 align:start size:88% position:13%
STEF: He needs clarity.
He needs direction.

00:36:18.408 --> 00:36:19.343
MATT: Yeah.

00:36:19.343 --> 00:36:21.445 align:start size:84% position:16%
STEF: There's no room
