00:38:42.919 --> 00:38:44.121
MATT: Yeah.

00:38:44.121 --> 00:38:46.757 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're gonna have your brother
Roosevelt come out, okay?

00:38:50.527 --> 00:38:52.863 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
Okay, let's see
what we got here. Okay.

00:38:52.863 --> 00:38:55.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
STEF: He is wagging his nub.
MATT: Good for him.

00:38:55.933 --> 00:38:57.168
STEF: Really sweet.

00:38:57.168 --> 00:38:58.669 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: That's cool,
'cause that's not what we saw

00:38:58.669 --> 00:39:00.571
last time between those two.

00:39:00.571 --> 00:39:03.873
Definitely more engaged,
a lot less deferential.

00:39:03.873 --> 00:39:06.644 align:start size:97% position:3%
STEF: Right.
Want to come in, bud? Alright.

00:39:06.644 --> 00:39:07.978
MATT: Okay, bring him in.

00:39:07.978 --> 00:39:09.146
STEF: Come on, Rosie.

00:39:09.146 --> 00:39:11.081
Yeah! Woo-hoo!

00:39:11.081 --> 00:39:13.117
Look at you go. Good boy!

00:39:13.117 --> 00:39:14.818
MATT: Wow.

00:39:14.818 --> 00:39:17.121 align:start position:0%
JUSTIN: I was kind of shocked
watching them walk into the pen,

00:39:17.121 --> 00:39:19.123
I kind of thought that
they were gonna revert

00:39:19.123 --> 00:39:20.590
back to the bad behaviors,

00:39:20.590 --> 00:39:23.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it was nice to see them
interact properly.

00:39:23.494 --> 00:39:25.329
STEF: Good boy!

00:39:25.329 --> 00:39:27.631 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: I feel like I'm watching
a hippo run in the wild

00:39:27.631 --> 00:39:29.166
for the first time.

00:39:29.166 --> 00:39:30.400 align:start size:81% position:19%
STEF: You are,
it's 'cause you are.

00:39:30.400 --> 00:39:32.436
MATT: Look at you.
That's beautiful.

00:39:32.436 --> 00:39:33.470
STEF: Good job.

00:39:33.470 --> 00:39:35.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
MATT:
Yes, we can do a walk, too.

00:39:35.239 --> 00:39:37.108 align:start position:0%
STEF: I got him. He's not gonna
bother you. I got him.

00:39:37.108 --> 00:39:37.908 align:start size:78% position:22%
MATT: Come on,
let's go this way.

00:39:37.908 --> 00:39:38.976
STEF: I got him.

00:39:38.976 --> 00:39:40.544
MATT: Good boy, Eisenhower.

00:39:40.544 --> 00:39:42.279
STEF: Truman, come on.

00:39:42.279 --> 00:39:45.482 align:start position:0%
We're doing a bulldog show here,
Truman.

00:39:45.482 --> 00:39:47.917 align:start position:0%
MATT: Hi, Truman. Let's get past
the fear a little bit.

00:39:47.917 --> 00:39:49.653
STEF: Good job! There you go.

00:39:49.653 --> 00:39:52.356
MATT: There we go.
Bulldogs on parade.

00:39:52.356 --> 00:39:53.691
CAITLYN: Go, go, go!

00:39:53.691 --> 00:39:55.359 align:start size:91% position:9%
MATT: Bulldogs on parade.
CAITLYN: Woo-hoo!

00:39:55.359 --> 00:39:57.193 align:start position:0%
STEF: You did it, bud! Come on.
MATT: Bulldogs on parade.

00:39:57.193 --> 00:39:58.662
CAITLYN: Good job. Take a break.

00:39:58.662 --> 00:40:01.064
MATT: Okay, fair enough.
You know he's maxed out.

00:40:01.064 --> 00:40:04.734 align:start position:0%
So there's a lot of great things
that Truman's demonstrated.

00:40:04.734 --> 00:40:08.672
Eisenhower's, you know, smelling
in ways that he hadn't before.

00:40:08.672 --> 00:40:12.109
Roosevelt seems way more
comfortable in his skin.

00:40:12.109 --> 00:40:14.612 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's a lot of benchmarks
here for them.

00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:18.449 align:start size:91% position:9%
It's small,
it doesn't look like much,

00:40:18.449 --> 00:40:22.252
but we keep seeing these
openings of possibilities.

00:40:22.252 --> 00:40:26.156 align:start position:0%
They're at the beginning of
the end of fighting ever again.

00:40:26.156 --> 00:40:27.691
JUSTIN: I totally
notice a difference

00:40:27.691 --> 00:40:29.960 align:start size:81% position:19%
in terms of smelling
the other dogs

00:40:29.960 --> 00:40:33.597 align:start size:97% position:3%
and not being attached to me,
not growling.

00:40:33.597 --> 00:40:35.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel great knowing
they'll be able to socialize

00:40:35.933 --> 00:40:39.537 align:start position:0%
with other dogs and not act
aggressively towards each other.

00:40:39.537 --> 00:40:40.704
It's amazing.

00:40:40.704 --> 00:40:43.273 align:start position:0%
MATT: You and Bryant gotta keep
doing the work in the home.

00:40:43.273 --> 00:40:44.374
JUSTIN: Yes.

00:40:44.374 --> 00:40:47.143 align:start size:97% position:3%
MATT: Just do copious amounts
of dog socialization.

00:40:47.143 --> 00:40:50.380
He's gotta keep coming with
some kind of regularity.

00:40:50.380 --> 00:40:52.382
The good news is that
the recovery works

00:40:52.382 --> 00:40:55.052
exponentially faster
than the damage does.

00:40:55.052 --> 00:40:57.688 align:start size:97% position:3%
If Bryant and Justin can stay
committed to this work,

00:40:57.688 --> 00:41:01.124
it is absolutely possible that
this beautiful bulldog family

00:41:01.124 --> 00:41:03.359 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
can have a happy
and safe life together,

00:41:03.359 --> 00:41:05.095 line:0%
which is all I want for them.

00:41:05.095 --> 00:41:07.097
Good boy, Eisenhower.

00:41:10.234 --> 00:41:11.234
STEF: Hey, how's it going?

00:41:11.234 --> 00:41:12.236
RAYHAN: Hi. Good. How are you?

00:41:12.236 --> 00:41:14.405 align:start size:78% position:22%
STEF: Come on out.
You guys ready?

00:41:14.405 --> 00:41:15.973
Hello, Mr. Pax.

00:41:15.973 --> 00:41:18.975 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Today we're doing
a follow-up session with Pax.

00:41:18.975 --> 00:41:21.845 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's interesting.
It's a slightly different bark.

00:41:21.845 --> 00:41:23.514 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I immediately noticed
a change in Pax.

00:41:23.514 --> 00:41:25.381
Coming in with Pax.

00:41:25.381 --> 00:41:26.850
His bark isn't as aggressive,

00:41:26.850 --> 00:41:28.652 align:start size:81% position:19%
he's not displaying
as much fear.

00:41:28.652 --> 00:41:29.686
He's not lunging.

00:41:29.686 --> 00:41:32.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to know how things
have been going

00:41:32.456 --> 00:41:34.191
since Matt came over.

00:41:34.191 --> 00:41:35.959 align:start size:97% position:3%
RIDDHI: Well, we've been
following a lot of the, like,

00:41:35.959 --> 00:41:38.128 align:start size:78% position:22%
only acknowledging
and reaffirming

00:41:38.128 --> 00:41:39.462
his positive behaviors.

00:41:39.462 --> 00:41:41.031 align:start size:91% position:9%
RAYHAN: Only touching him
when he's calm.

00:41:41.031 --> 00:41:42.866
RIDDHI: Good boy, Pax.

00:41:42.866 --> 00:41:44.134 align:start size:84% position:16%
RAYHAN: That seems
to have changed a lot.

00:41:44.134 --> 00:41:45.302
MATT: Excellent.

00:41:45.302 --> 00:41:46.770 align:start position:0%
RIDDHI: I'm finding he's making
those like right decisions,

00:41:46.770 --> 00:41:49.173
like laying down,
sitting quicker.

00:41:49.173 --> 00:41:52.842
STEF: So choosing calm,
self-soothing behaviors

00:41:52.842 --> 00:41:54.945
more quickly is what
you've been noticing.

00:41:54.945 --> 00:41:56.713
RIDDHI: Yeah, I would say
like a week and a half ago,

00:41:56.713 --> 00:41:58.715
I was walking both Pax and Emma,

00:41:58.715 --> 00:42:01.518 align:start size:91% position:9%
and we saw like three guys
with like five dogs,

00:42:01.518 --> 00:42:02.819 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then they were like,
"Oh, if you want,

00:42:02.819 --> 00:42:04.521
like we can do, like,
a little group walk

00:42:04.521 --> 00:42:05.789
around the whole park."

00:42:05.789 --> 00:42:06.857 align:start size:81% position:19%
And he got a lot of,
like, you know...

00:42:06.857 --> 00:42:07.924
RAYHAN: Socializing.

00:42:07.924 --> 00:42:09.093
RIDDHI: Socializing,
so it was really nice.

00:42:09.093 --> 00:42:10.861 align:start size:78% position:22%
STEF: I love that.
RIDDHI: Yeah.

00:42:10.861 --> 00:42:11.929
STEF: I love that so much.

00:42:11.929 --> 00:42:13.063
MATT: Have you ever had
an experience like that

00:42:13.063 --> 00:42:13.864
with him before?

00:42:13.864 --> 00:42:15.132
RAYHAN: No.
RIDDHI: No.

00:42:15.132 --> 00:42:17.667
STEF: That's awesome. I think
that's like a really big step

00:42:17.667 --> 00:42:21.071 align:start position:0%
for Pax and for the both of you
to take with him.

00:42:21.071 --> 00:42:23.407
MATT: The news on Pax
is really encouraging.

00:42:23.407 --> 00:42:26.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
This dog was so reactive,
I gotta see this for myself.

00:42:26.309 --> 00:42:29.812 align:start size:97% position:3%
I want to see him with
Stef's dog, Amala, off-leash.

00:42:29.812 --> 00:42:32.416
You can take leash off, Rayhan.

00:42:36.120 --> 00:42:39.456 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's great that you two
are not engaging,

00:42:39.456 --> 00:42:41.258
'cause that's part
of the makeup here.

00:42:41.258 --> 00:42:42.893 align:start size:97% position:3%
STEF: So this is his response
to Amala,

00:42:42.893 --> 00:42:44.728
which is to totally ignore.

00:42:44.728 --> 00:42:47.498
He's like, "I don't want
to mess with this girl,"

00:42:47.498 --> 00:42:50.567 align:start position:0%
and she leaves him alone,
and this is a comfortable place

00:42:50.567 --> 00:42:52.536
for them to be, and that's it.

00:42:52.536 --> 00:42:56.139
MATT: This is all part
of a more mature Pax,

00:42:56.139 --> 00:42:58.675 align:start size:81% position:19%
a dog that is
not only practicing

00:42:58.675 --> 00:43:01.011
consistently good
impulse control,

00:43:01.011 --> 00:43:05.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
but is making decisions
that are about not engaging,

00:43:05.248 --> 00:43:08.752 align:start size:88% position:13%
about self soothing,
about being deferential.

00:43:08.752 --> 00:43:11.655 align:start size:84% position:16%
He's not fighting
to get the muzzle off.

00:43:11.655 --> 00:43:13.724 align:start size:84% position:16%
You don't see tension
in the body,

00:43:13.724 --> 00:43:16.025
you know, there's not,
the eyes aren't weird.

00:43:16.025 --> 00:43:17.928
This I've never seen from Pax.

00:43:17.928 --> 00:43:18.996
STEF: I think it's amazing.

00:43:18.996 --> 00:43:21.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's an amazing leap
that he's made.

00:43:21.131 --> 00:43:24.300
MATT: He's clearly moving
into sustainable change.

00:43:24.300 --> 00:43:26.436
That dog came from
a horrific place.

00:43:26.436 --> 00:43:29.873 align:start position:0%
It tells me that there's
something inherent in this work

00:43:29.873 --> 00:43:31.741
that can help even a dog

00:43:31.741 --> 00:43:34.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's been as crippled
and underprivileged as Pax,

00:43:34.578 --> 00:43:36.179 align:start size:81% position:19%
that he can be safe
in this world,

00:43:36.179 --> 00:43:39.049
that he's not a bad dog,
and I want that for him.

00:43:39.049 --> 00:43:41.285 align:start size:91% position:9%
STEF: Really impressed
with the way that you guys

00:43:41.285 --> 00:43:44.755 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
have remained detached
this entire time

00:43:44.755 --> 00:43:47.157 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
with the ups and downs
this has taken.

00:43:47.157 --> 00:43:48.424 line:0%
MATT: Yeah.

00:43:48.424 --> 00:43:50.893 align:start position:0% line:0%
STEF: I think that you're making
all of this possible for him.

00:43:50.893 --> 00:43:52.929 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
MATT: Clearly.
STEF: Yeah.

00:43:52.929 --> 00:43:54.865 line:0%
RIDDHI: I'm very proud
of how far Pax has come.

00:43:54.865 --> 00:43:56.299 line:0%
Every day he gets better.

00:43:56.299 --> 00:43:57.434 line:0%
When I first came
to the Zen Dog,

00:43:57.434 --> 00:43:59.336 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
I was at like my wits' end
with him,

00:43:59.336 --> 00:44:01.672 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
I was like I'm gonna
have to, like, give him up.

00:44:01.672 --> 00:44:03.507 line:0%
I was really, really sad.

00:44:03.507 --> 00:44:05.875 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
RAYHAN: The Zen Dog definitely
gave Pax a second chance

00:44:05.875 --> 00:44:07.811 line:0%
at a functional, happy life.

